Working my way through the mines, I had lost my dog, and was very upset.
Fortunately, came across a figurine of an orge, which 2 turns later, was
named Fred :)  Now, it was no prob getting him a weapon, but I wanted to
armor hm as well.  I gathered a big pile of equipment (uncursed) and set
it in front of me.  Well, Fred crossed the pile several times, but he never
picked up armor and then wear it....he only dropped in nearby like a dog
or cat would.  After waiting too long with this, I decended with Fred to 
the next lever.  Fred immediately got diced (hit a lot), and I was killed
shortly later.

My comment is is that you should be able to tell your 'pet' to wear
armor and weild weapon, if appropiate.  OR let that be an option for pets
to wear armor if picked up (normal monsters do it all the time).
OR implement a '# give' command, where you give the piece of equipment
to the pet, which he immediately uses as approipate (drink potion, 
read scroll (if poss), wear ring/amulet, etc.)  

